From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Palmer <dodava@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:57:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mwifiex: Name the station interface wlan0

mwifiex names its station interface "mlan0". Nerves has no udev to
rename it, and VintageNetWiFi.quick_configure/2, the nerves_pack
defaults and most examples expect "wlan0". Use the usual name instead.

---
 drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c
@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@
 	rtnl_lock();
 	wiphy_lock(adapter->wiphy);
 	/* Create station interface by default */
-	wdev = mwifiex_add_virtual_intf(adapter->wiphy, "mlan%d", NET_NAME_ENUM,
+	wdev = mwifiex_add_virtual_intf(adapter->wiphy, "wlan%d", NET_NAME_ENUM,
 					NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(wdev)) {
 		mwifiex_dbg(adapter, ERROR,
